title: 'fatxpool: add transactions from retracted blocks to the mempool'

doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |-
      Transactions from retracted blocks were only resubmitted to the new view and never reached
      the mempool, so when the pool was at its limits they could later be pushed out by mempool
      transactions regardless of their priority. They are now added to the mempool as well, using
      the priority obtained while resubmitting them. When the mempool is full they go through the
      usual replacement path, so a higher priority retracted transaction evicts lower ones and a
      lower priority one is dropped.

      Retracted transactions are now also resubmitted when the newly enacted block already has a
      view, for example when it was imported as non best earlier or gets finalized while a sibling
      is the best block. Previously they were lost for that view and its descendants.

crates:
  - name: sc-transaction-pool
    bump: patch
